hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27685","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Akhbarana Sharik ibn Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah, from his uncle Imran ibn Talhah, from his mother Hamnah bint Jahsh, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I have menstruated a severe, unfamiliar bleeding. So he said: Stuff yourself with cotton. I said: It is severer than that; I gush it forth gushing. He said: Bind yourself and menstruate in each month, by the knowledge of Allah, six days or seven days, then wash once, and fast and pray twenty-three or twenty-four days, and wash for Fajr once, and delay Dhuhr and hasten Asr and wash once, and delay Maghrib and hasten Isha and wash once. And this is the more beloved of the two matters to me. And Yazid once did not say: And wash for Fajr once."
